      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VOUCHERS (1) is the one to beat after dropping out of BM60 company, with his seventh at this track last start better than it first appears given he was checked near the 800m and beaten only 2.5L. His Townsville second over the mile prior adds substance, and his strong track and trip record sets him up a treat. MR FERRARI (8) is the key danger off a much sharper BM62 fourth at Townsville, where he was beaten just under a length at big odds, and the BM55 grade relief brings him right into calculations. ELECTRIC BRAE (3) has a clear excuse for the Townsville failure after early interference, while her CL3 second at Bowen and 2kg claim keep her competitive. RUM RUMBLE (2) rises from a BM50 at Home Hill and a picnic-level lead-up, but the narrow heavy-track third and three placings from three tries around 1450m keep him in the mix. THUNDER BLAZE (5) got off the mark in style last time and while this is tougher he has upside and is worth keeping onside.",
